        "denialFound": "This is not a denial of this edge. It is the state's response to the audit it comes from. Scroll, citing the Hindustan Times, quotes WCD Additional Chief Secretary Ashok Shah: \"The transport of THR is mentioned by motorcycle, car, auto and tanker instead of trucks ... it was found in MP Agro's investigation that the above errors have been made in clerical form.\" He also called the report \"an interim one\". Source: https://scroll.in/latest/1032051/madhya-pradesh-large-scale-irregularities-found-in-nutrition-scheme-claims-audit-report. I found no response from MPSRLM or the plant federations, and there is no record that they were asked.",
        "innocentReading": "MP WCD runs a statewide THR programme with about 49.58 lakh registered beneficiaries (as of 2021). Production is spread across about seven plants that MPSRLM set up with a ₹141 cr advance. The AG's draft audit examined six of them. The edge simply records a state supply arrangement. Read innocently it implies neither exclusivity nor that these six plants supplied every beneficiary.",
        "reason": "This claim joins two separate facts from the sources. Fact 1 is the size of the statewide programme (49.58 lakh registered, per The Quint \"in 2021\"). Fact 2 is Scroll's list of six plants, which appears only in a sentence saying they claimed to supply 821 MT (₹4.95 cr) beyond their capacity. The label merges them into \"six plants supplied THR for 49.58 lakh beneficiaries, 2018–21\", which neither source says. Scroll itself refers to seven plants, and The Quint dates the 49.58 lakh figure to 2021, not 2018–21. The underlying award relationship (MP WCD/MPSRLM to the THR plants) is supported at reported tier. The label as written is not.",
