        "denialFound": "Yes. ThePrint, 7 Sep 2022 (https://theprint.in/india/no-corruption-in-nutrition-scheme-ag-audit-report-not-final-mp-home-minister/1119984/). MP Home Minister Narottam Mishra: \"There were no irregularities in the poshan-aahar programme\" and \"The report in question was not final.\" This is already recorded as contra c026. Scroll also quotes the state's reply to the audit: \"it was found in MP Agro's investigation that the above errors have been made in clerical form.\"",
        "innocentReading": "This is ordinary opposition messaging after a leaked draft AG audit. The state called the draft interim and put some findings down to clerical and transcription errors. The AG itself asked the state government for an independent-agency investigation. No FIR, EOW/Lokayukta case or central-agency action followed on the record in hand. A demand from an opposition party is not an enforcement action.",
        "reason": "Two problems, and either one is enough to refute. (1) Wrong predicate. The CONTRACT defines `enforce` as agency→subject (cancellation, suspension, freeze, investigation, sanction, debarment). A political party demanding a probe is none of these, so the edge implies an enforcement action that never happened. The CONTRACT also bars \"alleged\" as a stand-in predicate, and no predicate fits a political demand. (2) The sources back a looser version of the claim. INC did not demand a central-agency probe in the cited sources. TMC (Supriyo: \"Why not CBI for this?\") and CPI(M) (Yechury) did. INC made a Vyapam comparison and, per ThePrint, demanded Chouhan's resignation. Neither source attributes the ₹100+ cr figure or the phrase \"poshan scam\" to Congress. The Quint does not mention the opposition at all. The underlying facts (an opposition outcry and a demand for a central probe) are real and reported by Scroll with named quotes. They belong in a node description or the narrative at tier reported, not as an INC→mp-wcd enforce edge.",
