        "denialFound": "None found. The FPJ article carries no response from the WCD department or the state government (WebFetch: \"The article contains no government or WCD department response\"). Whether anyone was asked is not recorded, and sibling edge c029 already says so. CAG reports normally print the government's reply, but the report PDF was not located. A new web search could not be run because the session's search budget was exhausted.",
        "innocentReading": "District officers used local women's groups that had not completed formal registration or empanelment (for example on the state SHG/NRLM portal) so that meals kept reaching the anganwadis. This is a compliance and documentation lapse, not diversion, and the ₹8.1 cr may correspond to meals that were actually delivered. The article's separate findings do point beyond paperwork: 13 SHGs had no kitchen or office at the billed address, non-member men were cooking for pay, and stock registers were missing. But those findings attach to subsets, not to the whole ₹8.1 cr.",
