        "denialFound": "None found. The Tribune, Scroll (https://scroll.in/latest/1080421/ed-raids-eight-george-soros-linked-entities-in-bengaluru) and The News Minute (https://www.thenewsminute.com/karnataka/bengaluru-ed-raids-eight-locations-linked-to-george-soros-open-source-foundation) carry no statement from OSF, SEDF or Aspada, and none says it contacted them. So in the reports I checked they were not asked. I found no statement in the OSF newsroom or in Google News results. WebSearch was over budget, so the search for a response was partial.",
        "innocentReading": "SEDF invests in Indian for-profit companies through Aspada, which is its SEBI/RBI-regulated fund manager and wholly owned by a Mauritius entity. This is lawful FDI and can go through the automatic route. Consultancy fees paid to Indian advisory firms such as ASAR are ordinary services income. The 2016 prior-reference listing controls FCRA donations to NGOs, not FDI into companies. The funds contravene FEMA only if they can be shown to have paid for NGO activity in breach of end-use conditions. ED has asserted that through unnamed sources and has not proved it. No show-cause notice or adjudication order has been published.",
