        "denialFound": "No denial is needed or found, because the disclosure comes from GoI itself (the Finance Ministry annual report). The only contest is over the separate US$21m 'voter turnout' claim by DOGE and Trump. The same article reports the Finance Ministry report's statement that 'no funding was made for enhancing voter turnout' in the year, EAM Jaishankar calling the US claims 'concerning', and Congress (Jairam Ramesh) saying the US$21m was for Bangladesh. Source: https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/usaid-funded-7-projects-in-india-in-fy24-not-related-to-voter-turnout-govt-125022300390_1.html",
        "innocentReading": "This is a routine, publicly disclosed bilateral development programme: agriculture and food security, WASH, renewable energy, disaster management, health, forests and climate adaptation, and energy efficiency. It is coordinated by the DEA as nodal department and reported in the government's own annual report. Nothing in the claim implies wrongdoing.",
        "reason": "The Business Standard (PTI) article, which I opened (HTTP 200), supports the core figures word for word: \"Currently, seven projects worth a total budget of USD 750 million (approx.) are being implemented by USAID in partnership with Government of India,\" as per the Finance Ministry annual report for 2023-24. For the financial year 2023-24, an obligation of a total of USD 97 million (about Rs 825 crore) has been made by the US Agency for International Development (USAID) under the seven projects. 'reported' is the right tier: one wire story quoting a primary document the record admits was not opened. I tried to open the DEA report: curl to dea.gov.in failed TLS verification (exit 60, incomplete certificate chain), WebFetch got 503, and the proxy rejected finmin.nic.in. So no upgrade is possible now. PTI syndication elsewhere is the same wire, not an independent second outlet. The claim is not refuted, but it has three field errors, listed under corrections: the counterparty, the unsupported attribution of the rupee conversion, and the sector list.",
