        "denialFound": "LC denial of the substantive allegations is on the same page: \"LC denies all of the accusations and plans to appeal the MHA's decision in court\" (https://www.frontlinedefenders.org/en/case/cancellation-registration-lawyers-collective). It is already recorded as contra c035. On the media-briefing allegation I found no MHA response. Not asked by FLD; I did not verify whether MHA was asked elsewhere, because the search budget was exhausted.",
        "innocentReading": "The suspension is a routine enforcement step after an inspection that began with notices from November 2015. The \"media briefing\" may have been an ordinary press note or an official's comment, or the order may have been sent and a copy reached the press before it reached LC's office (a postal or courier lag). That would not be a deliberate briefing in breach of s.20. Section 20 covers information obtained through inspection of accounts, and whether announcing a suspension breaches it is disputed.",
