        "sourceCheck": "partially",
        "denialFound": "Yes, three denials. (1) Lawyers Collective's statement of 7 December 2016 \"denied the allegations listed in the cancellation order\" (https://www.frontlinedefenders.org/en/case/cancellation-registration-lawyers-collective). The June 2016 entry says: \"LC denies all of the accusations and plans to appeal.\" This is recorded as contra edge c035. (2) A specific rebuttal on the ASG ground: the remuneration was paid \"before she became the additional solicitor general and continued during and after the tenure with the permission of the Law Ministry\" (Scroll, https://scroll.in/latest/927454/cbi-files-case-against-indira-jaisings-ngo-lawyers-collective-for-alleged-fcra-violations). (3) The 2019 CBI FIR, LC said, had \"no basis in fact and in law\".",
        "innocentReading": "These are the government's asserted grounds and nobody has ruled on them. On the first ground, LC says the Law Ministry, the competent authority, approved the continued remuneration under the Law Officers (Terms and Conditions) Rules, and that MHA admitted this. If that is right, the \"government servant\" ground falls away. Communication costs of an honorary, unpaid UN mandate being reimbursed by the rapporteur's home NGO, and advocacy rallies, are routine NGO activities. Treating them as FCRA violations depends on contested readings of \"political activity\" and of the Rules. Business Standard reports that the Bombay HC granted Jaising and Grover interim protection in 2019 in the CBI case.",
        "reason": "The claim survives in substance. It correctly presents these as MHA allegations at tier \"alleged\" and has a contra edge (c035). FLD names the three grounds, and Scroll and Business Standard independently report them. The tier fits: these are government allegations that no court has ruled on. The attribution needs fixing, though. The cited source ties the three grounds to the 1 June 2016 suspension, not to the 27 November 2016 cancellation order. The source also does not contain \"ASG\" or the 2006-07 to 2013-14 window the record uses for its date test. Hence sourceCheck is \"partially\", not \"confirmed\".",
