          "1) `from`: change '2012-07-16' to '2012'. If month precision is wanted, cite a source other than FIDH that gives the date. Also remove the '2012-07-16 first CPSC suspension' wording from the minister entity's `d` (fcra-actions.json line ~1539). 2) `d`: delete 'UPA era (Chidambaram → Shinde)' or relabel it as our inference; keep 'UPA era'. 3) Text/lab: 'Three suspensions of CPSC FCRA registration between 2012 and 2014 (UPA), totalling 18 months (FIDH); Delhi HC ruled for CPSC 2014-03'. 4) Set `to` to '2014-03' as the end of the suspension series, and note that FIDH does not give the date the last suspension ended. 5) Set `supersededBy` to null. c083 (HC → MHA) is a separate edge and cannot replace the MHA → CPSC enforcement edge. Keep both and link them. 6) Add a contra per the wording rule: CPSC's HC challenge that succeeded in 2014-03 (FIDH), plus 'MHA grounds: 2014 complaint alleging unaccounted withdrawals (as described by FIDH); no MHA statement recorded, asked/not asked unknown'. 7) upgradeIf: the Delhi HC judgment of 2014-03 on CPSC's writ against the suspension. 8) Sibling fixes found along the way: in c084, the HC order of 28.11.2025 gives the refusal date as 29.10.2016 (FIDH says 29 Jan 2016). The same order (Amit Sharma J., W.P.(C) 10527/2016, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/150583269/) set aside the 2016 refusal and allowed CPSC to apply afresh, with a decision due within 90 days. That meets c085's killIf ('HC directs renewal'), and c084's 'case pending' is out of date."
