        "denialFound": "The Trust's response is in the source. Its senior counsel told the Delhi HC on 2024-04-05: \"They have to give us a personal hearing before they pass the order of cancellation. There was no hearing given to us.\" (https://www.devdiscourse.com/article/law-order/2878882-hc-seeks-centres-stand-on-plea-by-environics-trust-against-fcra-cancellation). The Trust is challenging the order, not denying it exists. MHA/Centre: the court asked for a reply within four weeks, but no public MHA statement was found. Asked (by the court); no reply on the public record.",
        "innocentReading": "The boring explanation: a routine FCRA regulatory action following a CBI FIR over 2018 transfers and alleged use of funds for purposes other than those declared. It sits in the same post-2020 wave of cancellations and non-renewals that hit thousands of associations. The edge claims nothing beyond the cancellation and the Trust's procedural objection, so this reading does not conflict with it.",
        "reason": "The one source, a PTI wire carried by Devdiscourse, states the exact fact, date and target, and records the Trust's response. A 2026 Delhi HC order confirms the litigation over Environics Trust's FCRA status is real and still pending, which rules out quashing so far. The claim is not refuted. It stays at reported rather than documented: syndicated copies of PTI are not independent outlets, the order text itself was not opened, and the 2026 order calls the action a renewal rejection, which leaves its legal type slightly unsettled. The search budget ran out, and the direct site searches that followed (LiveLaw, The Wire, Bar & Bench) found no second independent outlet.",
