        "denialFound": "None found, and the Trust was asked. PTI emailed Environics Trust about both the FIR (2024-01) and the chargesheet (2025-01): \"An email sent to ET by PTI seeking a response on the development remained unanswered by the time of filing this story.\" ThePrint (2024-01-19) also wrote: \"ThePrint has reached Environics Trust on email for comment. This report will be updated if and when a response is received.\" The only recorded position is a procedural one from counsel in the Delhi HC on 2024-04-05: \"They have to give us a personal hearing before they pass the order of cancellation. There was no hearing given to us\" (Devdiscourse/PTI). That is not a denial of the payments.",
        "innocentReading": "Dhinkia is in Jagatsinghpur district, which was reportedly among the Odisha coastal districts hit by Cyclone Amphan (May 2020). The same 711 villagers could have been genuinely cyclone-affected relief recipients and also participants in the long-running anti-JSW (formerly POSCO) agitation. A relief disbursement six months after the cyclone, made to residents of a protest village, fits both readings. CBI's case that the money was \"actually paid to the protesters for JSW agitation\" has not been tested in court.",
        "reason": "The one cited source (Devdiscourse, syndicated PTI copy, 2024-04-05) states the claim almost verbatim: \"According to the CBI, Environics Trust had allegedly transferred Rs 1,250 each in the bank accounts of 711 people on November 15, 2020, for distribution among Amphan cyclone-affected people in Odisha but actually the payments were made to protestors for JSW agitation at Dhinkia, Odisha.\" ThePrint (2024-01-19) confirms it independently. The claim is worded as an allegation, attributed to the CBI FIR and marked not adjudicated, so \"alleged\" is the correct tier. Nothing refutes it. The fixes needed are the actor field, a stale status (a chargesheet was filed 2025-01-24) and the contra, which should record that the Trust was asked and did not answer.",
