        "denialFound": "No denial. The party was asked and confirmed the cancellation. ET, 2023-09-14, Rahul Tripathi (https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/india/home-ministry-cancels-fcra-licence-of-bal-trust/articleshow/103643895.cms): \"A senior functionary of the trust confirmed that its FCRA licence has been cancelled but did not elaborate further.\" No public statement from Bal Raksha Bharat or Save the Children disputing the grounds was found. Further web search was blocked by the search budget.",
        "innocentReading": "This may be a routine refusal or cancellation in the 30 Sept 2023 re-registration round after the 2020 FCRA amendments, for a technical or compliance reason (for example, the post-2020 SBI New Delhi FCRA account or utilisation-for-administration limits). It need not be a finding of misuse. The source's 'misuse or diversion' sentence is generic background on the law (\"Any misuse or diversion of foreign funds by NGOs is considered a violation\"). It is not a ground attributed to this NGO. The ₹163.18 crore figure is total bank receipts from an audited report. It shows size, not wrongdoing, and the source does not explicitly call it foreign contribution.",
        "reason": "The source holds up. Outlook states the cancellation and the amount: \"Bal Raksha Bharat's licence has been revoked... it had received Rs 163.18 crore in its bank accounts and Rs 66.66 lakh worth of in-kind contributions for the year 2021-22, ET reported\". Outlook says 'reportedly' and relays ET's story rather than reporting independently. The ET original (Rahul Tripathi, ET Bureau, 2023-09-14) has 'officials said' sourcing and the exact figure '₹163,18,59,530'. It also has the NGO's own confirmation (\"A senior functionary of the trust confirmed that its FCRA licence has been cancelled\"). That is one credible outlet with named sourcing plus a party confirmation, which fits 'reported'. It is not 'documented': there are no two independent outlets (Outlook is derivative), and no MHA order or FCRA portal entry was opened. Nothing found shows the order was quashed.",
