        "denialFound": "Only the movement's general denial is on record. Tribune 2012-02-25 quotes S.P. Udayakumar of PMANE: \"It is unfortunate that the Prime Minister has made the allegations without any documentary proof. We strongly deny his observation that the agitation is being funded by other countries.\" DH 2012-02-28 reports that Udayakumar sent a legal notice to the PM calling the imputation \"totally false\" (https://www.deccanherald.com/content/230728/4-ngos-booked-funding-protests.html). No response from the three unnamed associations exists, because they were never named; whether they were asked is unknown. The contrary official account is Chidambaram's (freezes and cases, no cancellations): https://www.deccanherald.com/india/pc-says-more-ngos-scanner-2317244",
        "innocentReading": "Narayanasamy was not the minister responsible for FCRA. He may have conflated account freezes or suspensions of prior permission with \"cancelled licences\", or counted routine 2011-12 cancellations for non-filing of FC returns among Tamil Nadu associations that happened to be under the same scrutiny. The official version that followed (four accounts frozen, criminal cases, no cancellations mentioned) fits a picture in which no Kudankulam-specific FCRA cancellation had been completed by 24 February 2012.",
        "reason": "The Tribune URL loads, and it does carry the sentence \"the home ministry had cancelled licences of three of the 12 NGOs\". But the claim turns a second-hand statement by a minister from another ministry (MoS PMO/Personnel Narayanasamy) into an MHA enforcement act. It also turns \"operating licences\" into \"FCRA registrations\". The Home Minister's own account five days later describes four NGOs with frozen accounts and criminal cases and mentions no cancellations. Contemporaneous DH reporting on 24 and 28 February does not corroborate any cancellation. As worded, the edge states as fact something that only one relayed ministerial assertion supports, and the responsible ministry's account does not match it. As an MHA enforce edge it should be alleged, carrying a contra. Keep it at reported only if it is recast as Narayanasamy's statement.",
