        "denialFound": "Yes, in the same source. PMANE's S.P. Udayakumar (Chennai, 2012-02-24): \"It is unfortunate that the Prime Minister has made the allegations without any documentary proof. We strongly deny his observation that the agitation is being funded by other countries.\" (https://www.tribuneindia.com/2012/20120225/main2.htm). This is already recorded as contra fcra-actions:c098. Arun Jaitley (BJP) and D. Raja (CPI; the Tribune prints \"A. Raja\") asked the government to make the evidence public. The Tribune reports only that the NGOs \"took a strong exception\". The individual associations were not named, so whether they were asked is unknown.",
        "innocentReading": "Several Tuticorin/Tirunelveli church and social-service associations were long-standing FCRA-registered recipients of Western church and development funding for relief, fishing-community and post-tsunami work. Local anti-nuclear mobilisation drew on the same parish networks. The overlap in geography and personnel is enough to fit the PM's remark without any foreign funds being diverted to the agitation. The statement is also consistent with political pressure to commission a stalled Indo-Russian project.",
        "reason": "The substance survives as an allegation. The quoted sentence appears in the Tribune: \"these NGOs, mostly I think based in the United States, dont appreciate the need for our country to increase the energy supply\". The \"US and Scandinavian\" funding wording is in the PM's primary Science interview. The claim is dated inside his tenure, and a denial is recorded (c098). No adjudicated finding of diversion appears in any opened source, so alleged is the correct tier. The edge is mis-encoded, though. pred=enforce with s=wel:manmohan-singh says the PM took an enforcement action against the Kudankulam-linked associations. He did not: he gave a magazine interview aimed at foreign NGOs. The enforcement (3 of 12 licences cancelled, an MHA probe) is MHA's and is already edge c096. The \"Scandinavian\" attribution in the Tribune belongs to Narayanasamy.",
