        "reason": "The core edge holds. Both cited sources state the figure, each attributing it to the TOI analysis. TNM: \"Believers Church India and World Vision India which featured third and fourth on the list, declared foreign contributions of Rs 342.63 crore and Rs 319.26 crore respectively, the TOI report stated.\" Asianet: \"Believers Church, which featured third on the list, received foreign contributions of Rs 342.63 crore\". Both derive from one TOI report, so they are not independent, and \"reported\" is the right tier.\n\nThe claim text fails on its second half, in two ways.\n(1) Neither cited source mentions Last Hour Ministry, Love India Ministries or ₹1,348.65 cr. Asianet's headline says only \"over Rs 1000 cr\". The entity note's \"(Asianet citing TOI)\" is a misattribution. The figures actually appear in Light of Truth (https://lightoftruth.in/believers-church-barred-receiving-foreign-funds/): \"The Believers Church ... and associated organisations had received a whopping Rs 1,348.65 crore ... Ayana Charitable Trust ... Rs 826.27 crore. Believers Church had received Rs 342.64 crore, Last Hour Ministry Rs 103.51 crore and Love India Ministries Rs 76.23 crore during FY16.\"\n(2) ₹1,348.65 cr is the four-body total including Ayana (826.27+342.64+103.51+76.23 = 1,348.65). \"Group with Last Hour and Love India ₹1,348.65 cr\" implies those three bodies add up to ₹1,348.65 cr, but they add up to only ₹522.38 cr. That is a false conjunction.\nThere is also a ₹0.01 cr discrepancy for Believers itself between sources (342.63 vs 342.64).",
