        "denialFound": "None found. MHA was not asked. The \"non-reconciliation\" is our own inference and has never been put to MHA. No contrary reporting found.",
        "innocentReading": "RS Q.3253 (d) reads: \"Section 14 ... provides for cancellation of certificate of FCRA registration of an association for violations of provisions of the Act ... 1,828 associations have been cancelled under section 14 ... due to violation of the provisions of the Act and rules made thereunder.\" Section 14 is the Act's only cancellation route. Failing to file FC-4 returns breaches s.18 read with Rule 17, which is a \"violation of the Act and rules\". So cancellations for non-filing are s.14 \"violation\" cancellations. Inactivity cancellations also fall under s.14 (s.14(1)(c): defunct or no reasonable activity). The JPC breakdown splits s.14 cancellations by ground: non-filing 91.3%, inactive 7.9%, substantive \"legal violations\" 0.4%. The Q.3253 figure of 1,828 is the s.14 total for 2020–23 across all grounds. The two classifications nest; they do not conflict. Since 1,828 is about 8.3% of 21,983, the numbers are consistent with each other.",
