        "denialFound": "Not applicable. The figures are MHA's own, presented to the JPC, and the claim accuses no one. On the related bill, the government denied that it targets minorities, saying the legislation \"is not religion-specific and is aimed at regulating foreign contributions\" (same ThePrint article). That denial is not relevant to this arithmetic.",
        "innocentReading": "The boring explanation fits completely. Money from abroad was flat in dollars and fell in real rupee terms. The registration count halved mainly because dormant or non-compliant registrants were purged (91.3% of all cancellations to date were for non-filing, plus 7.9% for inactivity) and because registrations lapsed at renewal. The 'rise' is an artefact of measuring in nominal rupees. The existing innocentReading wording also needs care. Non-filing is a proxy for dormancy, not the same thing: MHA lists \"inactive\" (7.9%) as a separate ground, so not every non-filer is proven dormant. The fall in the active count (−14,556) also includes non-renewals and is offset by new registrations. It is not the same thing as the 21,983 cancellations.",
