        "denialFound": "None found in the record. Neither the government nor the BJP was asked. The government's stated rationale (fixing the definition of foreign source for Indian companies with foreign shareholding, per the Finance Bill 2016/2018 memoranda) is not retrieved or cited. Record as: No response recorded — asked/not asked unknown.",
        "innocentReading": "The retrospective change lined up the FCRA's 'foreign source' test with FEMA foreign-investment limits. That way, Indian-incorporated companies with foreign shareholding would not count as foreign sources for any recipient. The 2018 extension to 1976 closed the gap left because the 2016 fix covered only the 2010 Act, and the Delhi HC finding concerned the 1976 Act period. On this reading, shielding BJP and INC was the effect of a general definitional fix, not its stated purpose. On the other side, the benefit to both parties and the timing are real, and critics call the purpose self-serving.",
        "reason": "The only cited source (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_Bond_Scheme, which redirects to 'Electoral bonds') does not say what the claim says. Its sentence is: \"...the retrospective amendments made to the Foreign Currency Regulation Act (FCRA) by the government, on two separate occasions, in an effort to shield the BJP and the Congress from prosecution for FCRA violations, as determined by the Delhi High Court.\" It mentions no 'Finance Act 2018' and no '1976'. The underlying citation (JSCdh) is a Deccan Herald opinion column dated 5 Feb 2019 by Jagdeep S. Chhokar, an ADR co-founder. ADR is a litigant in the political-funding cases, which makes Chhokar a named interested party. The column says the government amended the FCRA \"not once but twice, in attempts to save the BJP and the Congress\" and also gives no year or 1976 date. So the specifics are unsourced, and the motive (\"to shield\") rests on an interested party's opinion column quoted through Wikipedia. That meets 'alleged', not 'reported'. The fact itself is very probably true and could be documented from the Gazette text of the Finance Act 2018 (Act 13 of 2018). But no such source is in the record, and I could not retrieve one.",
