        "denialFound": "None found; whether anyone was asked is unknown. Neither The Hindu (3 Feb 2018) nor The Wire's Finance Bill 2018 piece records a Congress or government comment. The Wire notes that in Dec 2016 the BJP's counsel Shyam Divan told the SC the appeals were unnecessary because of the 2016 amendment. That is a statement of legal position, not a denial. I found no Congress statement opposing or defending the 2018 clause. My web search budget was exhausted, so this is not a finding that no statement exists.",
        "innocentReading": "The government's stated rationale for 2016 was to align FCRA's \"foreign source\" test with FDI limits, so that a company within permitted foreign-investment caps is treated as Indian. On this reading the 2018 back-dating removes an inconsistency between the 1976 and 2010 regimes for every entity, not only the two parties. That reading and the \"shield\" reading predict the same statutory text. The shield characterisation comes from the press (The Hindu: \"a move that will benefit the ruling BJP and the Congress\"; The Wire: \"get-out-of-jail card\"), not from the statute. It is well grounded because the only live proceedings it affected were the Delhi HC findings against those two parties.",
