        "innocentReading": "Vedanta is one of India's largest mining and metals groups, with operations in states ruled by several different parties. It spread its bond purchases across the BJP, the Congress (its largest single recipient among opposition parties, ₹125 cr) and the BJD (₹40 cr, the ruling party in Odisha, where it runs alumina operations). That pattern fits hedged corporate political giving across whoever governs its operating states. Large firms with many projects almost always have some probe or clearance pending, so the probe overlap would appear whether or not there was any quid pro quo.",
