        "denialFound": "Yes. Reliance denied Qwik is its subsidiary. The source says: 'the third biggest donor - Qwik Supply Chain - was accused of being a subsidiary of Reliance Industries, a charge Reliance denied. However, the company's registration details indicated a connection.' (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_bonds, the target of the Electoral_Bond_Scheme redirect). That sentence cites NDTV, headlined 'Reliance Says Not Its Subsidiary' (https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/reliance-linked-qwik-supply-3rd-largest-electoral-bond-buyer-reliance-says-not-its-subsidiary-5245705), and Reuters, 15 Mar 2024 (https://www.reuters.com/world/india/qwik-top-buyer-indian-electoral-bonds-is-affiliated-ambanis-reliance-filings-2024-03-15/). Both primaries returned 403/401 and the web.archive.org copy reset the connection, so I could not quote Reliance's exact words. Nobody appears to have asked Reliance about foreign ownership or FCRA, and no source raises it.",
