        "denialFound": "No specific denial of \"steering\" was found, and I cannot tell whether the government was ever asked. The government's framing is on the record in PIB 1560246: the jury \"comprising the Chief Justice of India, Justice Ranjan Gogoi, Speaker of LokSabha Smt. Sumitra Mahajan, Leader of the single largest Opposition Party in LokSabha Shri. Mallikarjuna Kharge and Member of Parliament, Shri L.K. Advani after detailed discussions on 16th January, 2019 unanimously decided to select the above organisation/persons\" (https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1560246). I could not check contrary reporting, such as the Congress criticism of the 2021 Gita Press award: the web search budget was used up and no URL was opened.",
        "innocentReading": "The Gandhi Peace Prize is chosen by a statutory jury that includes the opposition. The 2015–18 batch was decided unanimously with Kharge (INC) on the jury, and each winner runs a large service network whose scale can be checked. Hindu-cultural or religious laureates also appear under NDA-I (Ramakrishna Mission 1998, Bharatiya Vidya Bhavan 2002), so the pattern is not specific to 2014 onward. DRI's KVK follows ICAR's routine NGO-host model and appears to predate 2014, given DRI's Chitrakoot work since 1972/2005. As for grants, the lack of a recipient list is a transparency gap that affects both periods equally. It does not show favouritism.",
