        "denialFound": "Greenpeace India, spokesperson Abhishek Pratap, in Deccan Herald/IANS on 2014-06-11 (https://www.deccanherald.com/india/greenpeace-rejects-ib-report-swears-2210733): \"We are not aware of any IB report criticising our work ... How can the IB come to that conclusion? We have never been served any notice for violating the provisions of the Foreign Contribution Act.\" He also confirmed that Greenpeace paid for the TISS and IIT-Bombay studies (he said IIT-Bombay, not IIT-Delhi). He denied supporting AAP candidates. The response was sought and is on record. The IB's cost method was never published and has not been defended in public.",
        "innocentReading": "The IB report is an internal threat assessment. Its headline number is an unsourced estimate (\"does not mention how it arrived at the percentage\", TNM). Its financial data are lawful FCRA-declared receipts (\"no mention of any money that has come through illegal means\"). The project delays at Kudankulam, POSCO and Niyamgiri also have domestic causes: land acquisition, forest-rights rulings (the Supreme Court's 2013 Niyamgiri gram sabha decision), and litigation. Foreign funding is one input among many, not a demonstrated cause.",
