        "denialFound": "Yes, found. (1) ThePrint/PTI, 7 Sep 2022: \"The Madhya Pradesh government on Wednesday denied irregularities in implementation of a supplementary nutrition scheme and said the Accountant General's audit report on the programme was not final\". Home Minister Narottam Mishra also cited the MP 15 AV 3835 vs MP 15 LA 3835 transcription error. https://theprint.in/india/no-corruption-in-nutrition-scheme-ag-audit-report-not-final-mp-home-minister/1119984/ (2) Scroll, 5 Sep 2022: WCD ACS Ashok Shah called them clerical errors, citing \"MP Agro's investigation\", and said \"the audit report is an interim one\". https://scroll.in/latest/1032051/... No response from SHG federations or MPSRLM was found, and nothing shows they were asked.",
        "innocentReading": "This was a draft or interim AG report. Some of the vehicle findings were transcription errors (AV vs LA plates). The ₹110.83 cr is a computed exposure from inconsistent beneficiary counts, not traced money (\"would have led to\"). The ₹141 cr MPSRLM advance is an unrecovered advance, not proven theft. The 2026 CAG finding is about individual unregistered SHGs in 7 of 13 sampled districts supplying ₹8.1 cr of hot cooked meals. That is a registration and eligibility breach, not proof of a federation-run THR fraud.",
        "reason": "The \"₹100+ crore\" element holds only as an allegation. It comes from an unfinalised AG draft, reported by The Quint (\"alleged high levels of corruption of more than Rs 100 crore, a document accessed by The Quint\") and by Scroll via NDTV/HT, and the state explicitly denied it. The \"run through SHG federations\" element appears in none of the four sources. It is the file's own join: an MPSRLM advance for plants, plus a WCD beneficiary-data loss, plus a 2026 hot-cooked-meal finding about unregistered individual SHGs. None of those says SHG federations ran a THR scam. The narrative's \"contested\" status and its strongestCounter are honest. But the claim sentence as worded attributes the scam to SHG federations with no source, so it is refuted in that form. Reworded to drop the federation attribution, it survives at the alleged tier with the contra already recorded.",
