          "narratives[4].strongestCase: remove \"(₹35,968 cr unutilised balances alone)\" or rephrase it as \"total unutilised FC across all registrants in 2024-25 was ₹35,968 cr (MHA to JPC); the share held by cancelled/ceased registrants is not published\". Also add PRS's key issues: non-renewal now triggers vesting; partly-FC assets vest entirely; no way to leave FCRA without losing assets; the Rs 10 lakh/2-year utilisation rule can trigger loss; no appeal or hearing on renewal denial. narratives[4].strongestCounter: qualify \"s.15 has vested such assets since 2010\" to \"s.15 has vested assets of cancelled (and, since 2020, surrendered) registrants in a State-prescribed authority since 2010; the Bill adds cessation, a central Designated Authority, permanent vesting and sale to the CFI\". Also add the government response: rejects the minority-targeting charge, says the Bill is not religion-specific, and that places of worship cannot be converted (PTI 18 Sep 2026; PIB 22 Jul 2026). Add the opposition's allegation (PTI: provisions \"will choke legitimate funding for Christian NGOs\") as the named party making the church framing. Keep it as a narrative only. It must not become an edge that names a religion as a target or actor. Keep status \"contested\", with the component facts at the documented tier. For consistency with PRS, note that the PIB figure of \"nearly 20,000 cancelled\" differs from PRS's 22,498."
